course: dictionary
lesson: 8684
title: Seep: slow, quiet flow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To seep means to flow slowly, a little at a time, through small holes, cracks or gaps. Water does not gush or splash when it seeps. It creeps. «Picture a shell sinking into soft mud at the bottom of the sea; more mud piles on top, and over millions of years water full of dissolved minerals seeps through.» The words over millions of years tell you the water moves very slowly.
explain: Seep can also be used for things that are not liquids. «On a winter night water seeps into a tiny crack» shows the water getting into a gap without anyone noticing. A feeling or an idea can seep in too: it slowly spreads into your mind, like fear seeping in when you are alone in the dark. Light, cold and smells can seep in through a gap in the same quiet way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. If the sentence still makes sense with the words «trickled slowly through», then seep probably means the same. Look for clue words like slowly, a little at a time, through, and into. These tell you the movement is quiet and gradual, not sudden.
fact: Seep is a verb: seep, seeps, seeped, seeping.
fact: «Seep» means to flow slowly through small holes or cracks, a little at a time.
fact: Water seeping through soil, sand and rock is how rain gets underground and how wells fill.
fact: Used for feelings and ideas, «seep in» means slowly spreading into someone's mind.
fact: Phrases to know: «seep in», «seep through», «seep out», «seep into».
exercise: «The water seeped through the cracks in the old wall, one drop at a time.» What does seeped mean here? | Turned into steam and vanished | Froze solid into ice | *Flowed slowly through small gaps | Shot out with great force
exercise: «Fear seeped into Maya's mind as the house grew dark.» What does seeped into mean here? | Was shouted loudly for everyone to hear | *Slowly spread into her mind | Burst out suddenly | Was wiped clean away
exercise: «On a winter night water seeps into a tiny crack, freezes, swells and pushes the crack wider.» What makes the crack grow? | *Water freezing and swelling | Tyres driving over it | Mud piling on top of it | The sun melting it
test: «Light can seep in through a gap under the door.» What does seep in mean here? | *Comes in slowly through a gap | Stays outside all night | Is painted on the door | Bursts in with a loud bang
test: Which sentence uses seep correctly? | «The loud bell seeped across the whole field.» | «The team seeped the ball into the goal with a shout.» | «She seeped the cake into the oven.» | *«Cold air seeped in under the door all night.»
exam: «Cold seeps are places where gas and oil leak from the sea floor.» Which word means nearly the same as seep here? | *leak | sparkle | bounce | freeze
